  "id": "hip-adduction",
  "name": "Hip Adduction",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain hip-adduction isolation. The roster owns the original unilateral supported standing band fixture, one exact bilateral Technogym seated isotonic-machine fixture at eighty degrees of hip flexion, and a hand-supported standing low-cable fixture. Their support, start and endpoint, knee posture, resistance, path constraint, and cadence remain branch-specific. The visible adductor-longus and brevis region is primary, gracilis, adductor magnus, and pectineus are secondary, and the trunk and pelvis roles remain categorical stabilizers. Magnus and pectineus credit is a categorical transfer from their shared adduction capability and Lovell's resisted isometric-adduction measurements to these dynamic fixtures, not exact-fixture EMG or a recruitment ranking. The cable fixture follows the Life Fitness poster; holding slight hip flexion for foot clearance and choosing the front-of-stance-foot endpoint are disclosed catalog clarifications, not measured joint angles. Cable role transfer is categorical anatomy and mechanics, not direct cable EMG. Other machines, unsupported cables, Copenhagen, squeeze, rotated, closed-chain, and multi-joint variants remain outside this contract.",
